---
import Layout from "../../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import EvaluationSim from "../../../components/simulations/EvaluationSim.astro";
---

<Layout
  path="/teaching/data-science-fundamentals/model-evaluation"
  title="Model Evaluation: Interactive Practice — Ahmad Fathan Hidayatullah"
  description="Interactive practice on confusion matrices, precision, recall, F1-score, generalisation and cross-validation, with a guess-first mode and full answer keys."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Data Science Fundamentals · Evaluation"
    title="Model Evaluation Practice"
    lede="Three short exercises: read a confusion matrix, choose the right metric for an application, then diagnose overfitting and underfitting."
  />

  <div class="container-site py-10">
    <nav class="mb-6 text-sm text-muted" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/teaching" class="font-medium text-primary hover:text-primary-dark">Teaching</a>
      <span class="mx-1.5">/</span>
      <a href="/teaching/data-science-fundamentals" class="font-medium text-primary hover:text-primary-dark">Data Science Fundamentals</a>
      <span class="mx-1.5">/</span>
      <span>Model Evaluation</span>
    </nav>

    <EvaluationSim />

    <section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">How to use this page</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-muted marker:text-primary">
        <li><b class="text-ink">Guess mode</b> is on by default. At every step you commit to an answer first; wrong options are crossed out and given a hint.</li>
        <li><b class="text-ink">Exercise 1</b>: 500 patients, 50 of them sick. Name the four cells, then compute the four metrics and see why accuracy misleads.</li>
        <li><b class="text-ink">Exercise 2</b>: three applications. Decide whether a false positive or a false negative costs more, and pick the metric that follows.</li>
        <li><b class="text-ink">Exercise 3</b>: three models. Compare training and testing scores, diagnose each one, and check the cross-validation mean.</li>
        <li>Use the arrow keys to move between steps, and the numbered circles to jump straight to one. The last step is a full answer key for each exercise.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
